{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #400: declared status 'open'. Formalized: yes. For any $k\\geq 2$ let $g_k(n)$ denote the maximum value of\\[(a_1+\\cdots+a_k)-n\\]where $a_1,\\ldots,a_k$ are integers such that $a_1!\\cdots a_k! \\mid n!$. Can one show that\\[\\sum_{n\\leq x}g_k(n) \\sim c_k x\\log x\\]for some constant $c_k$? Is it true that there is a constant $c_k$ such that for almost all $n<x$ we have\\[g_k(n)=c_k\\log x+o(\\log x)?\\] Current best: Erd\\H{o}s and Graham write that it is easy to show that $g_k(n) \\ll_k \\log n$ always, but the best possible constant is unknown. Prize: no. Tags: factorials, number theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_0bd85fb879720ed8209512e634ed419d73e241a76af14c098a08dd725310f253","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:400","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_b2da6a944f70ad72","object_root":"sha256:a9ed5b9ba664a5ec0fc193e8d9c9832038b4ee619d2b4c15ca40e4cca801f140","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record",